      'Wisdom on power and trust: "put not your trust in princes... in whom there is no help" (Psalm 146:3) -- no one should hold unchecked power; judge by FRUITS (Matthew 7:20), not words (Titus 1:16).',
      'Discernment as the standing posture: "prove all things; hold fast that which is good" (1 Thessalonians 5:21); "try the spirits" (1 John 4:1) -- test every claim, from hype to doom.',
      'The real "alignment problem," named biblically: power and knowledge without wisdom -- "knowledge puffeth up, but charity edifieth" (1 Corinthians 8:1); "the fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom" (Proverbs 9:10).',
