    levels: {
      child: 'You may have heard about AI -- computers that can talk, draw, and answer questions. Some very smart people are building AI to be more and more powerful, really fast, and a few of them are worried it could get out of control. Here is the good news you never have to forget: GOD is bigger than any computer, and He is in charge of everything -- "he changeth the times and the seasons" (Daniel 2:21). So we do not have to be scared! The Bible tells a story about people who built a giant tower to make themselves famous and powerful without God (it is called Babel) -- and God was not worried at all. We should be wise about new tools -- use them for good things, and always check if what people say is really true (the Bible says "prove all things," 1 Thessalonians 5:21). And remember the most important rule for building ANYTHING: "except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain" (Psalm 127:1) -- if God is not in it, it will not really last. So do not be afraid of AI, and do not treat it like it is God either. Be wise, be kind, and trust the One who holds tomorrow.',
      teen: 'This is one of the biggest conversations of your generation, so let’s meet it with a clear head. Daniel Kokotajlo, who used to research the future of AI at OpenAI, warns that AI is starting to improve ITSELF -- an AI helping build a smarter AI, in a loop he thinks could "explode" in capability -- and that a few companies (he names OpenAI, Anthropic, and others) are in an intense RACE to get there first, often in secret, with what he estimates is a real chance of catastrophe. Handle it in tiers: the fast progress and the safety-vs-race tension are real and worth taking seriously; but the exact odds and dates (superintelligence by 2027? 2040? a "70%" doom number?) are his FORECASTS -- educated guesses, not facts, so hold them loosely. Now here is the wild part: the Bible already described this shape. At Babel, humanity built a self-amplifying tower to "make us a name," needing no God -- and the LORD said, "now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do" (Genesis 11:4-6). Sound familiar? So what’s the move? NOT panic, and NOT worshiping the tech like it’s a savior. Three anchors. (1) God runs history -- "he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings" (Daniel 2:21); "He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh" (Psalm 2:4) -- "God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind" (2 Timothy 1:7). (2) Don’t trust hype OR concentrated power -- "put not your trust in princes... in whom there is no help" (Psalm 146:3); judge people "by their fruits" (Matthew 7:20), by what they actually DO, not their slogans. (3) The deepest issue isn’t smarter machines, it’s the ancient one -- power without wisdom: "knowledge puffeth up, but charity edifieth" (1 Corinthians 8:1); "the fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom" (Proverbs 9:10). Use the tools, prove every claim (1 Thessalonians 5:21), serve real people with them -- and remember, "except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain" (Psalm 127:1).',
      senior: 'For the seasoned believer, this lesson asks you to bring a lifetime of discernment to the newest tower on the plain. Daniel Kokotajlo, a former OpenAI researcher, describes artificial intelligence approaching a threshold where systems improve THEMSELVES -- AIs conducting the research that trains better AIs, a recursive loop he fears could become an "intelligence explosion" -- driven by a small set of powerful labs (he names OpenAI, Anthropic, and others) locked in a competitive race, guarding their methods as trade secrets, using non-disparagement clauses and public-relations narratives to control the story. He does not trust the leaders with "that much power," and forecasts a grave risk of catastrophe on the default path, offering instead a "Plan A" of slowing down, full transparency, international agreements, and a citizens’ dividend against economic displacement. Receive it in the three tiers the Word and honesty require. What is ESTABLISHED -- the rapid advance, the genuine tension between safety and the race, the documented fact that he walked away from equity rather than sign a clause silencing him -- state plainly. What is FORECAST -- the odds, the timelines, whether superintelligence arrives at all -- hold as his estimate, not settled fact; we do not fabricate certainty, in either direction. And what is a judgment of MOTIVE -- his charge that the leaders’ safety talk is mere rationalization -- attribute to him as his opinion; Scripture forbids us to presume another man’s heart, even as it hands us the very rule he reaches for: "by their fruits ye shall know them" (Matthew 7:20), and "they profess that they know God; but in works they deny him" (Titus 1:16) -- judge by the observable deed, not the press release. Now the deep frame, and it is older than Silicon Valley. Humanity has raised a self-amplifying tower before, to "make us a name" and to need no God -- and the LORD’s words over Babel fall with uncanny weight on a self-improving machine: "this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do" (Genesis 11:6). Its taproot is the serpent’s oldest offer, "ye shall be as gods" (Genesis 3:5). Against this, teach the young a posture that is neither the world’s panic nor its worship of the machine. First, the Sovereign holds the times: "he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise" (Daniel 2:21); "there are many devices in a man’s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand" (Proverbs 19:21); "He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh" (Psalm 2:4) -- therefore "God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind" (2 Timothy 1:7). Second, put no ultimate trust in men or their institutions: "put not your trust in princes, nor in the son of man, in whom there is no help" (Psalm 146:3); "it is better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in princes" (Psalm 118:9) -- and this is exactly why no lab, and no nation, should hold unchecked power. Third, his call for TRANSPARENCY the Word blesses: "there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed" (Luke 12:2); "he that doeth truth cometh to the light, that his deeds may be made manifest" (John 3:21); "have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them" (Ephesians 5:11) -- test every safety claim, "prove all things" (1 Thessalonians 5:21). Fourth, name the true "alignment problem": it is not merely aligning machines to human values -- human values themselves are fallen -- it is the ancient gap of power and knowledge without the fear of God: "knowledge puffeth up, but charity edifieth" (1 Corinthians 8:1); "the fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom" (Proverbs 9:10). And fifth, hold the philosophy of technology this house was given: a tool exists to make the person more able to follow The Way and to serve the neighbor, never to extract from him -- dominion is stewardship (Genesis 1:28), so use these tools toward people, and love those whose work and lives are disrupted (Galatians 6:10). We plan wisely -- 2027, 2040, whatever the year -- but "ye know not what shall be on the morrow. For what is your life? It is even a vapour... For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will" (James 4:14-15). So build, and be watchful; test everything; trust no tower and no prince with your soul -- and rest the whole matter where it has always belonged: "except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it" (Psalm 127:1).',
    },
