        'The servant-king is the cure: “whosoever will be great... shall be your minister” (Mark 10:43-45; Mark 9:35; John 13:14). To be king in His house, become a servant.',
        'Still want GREATNESS — the balance: excellence is commanded (Colossians 3:23; Ecclesiastes 9:10; Daniel 6:3), and it is measured. But strife LOWERS quality; joy is the engine — “the joy of the LORD is your strength” (Nehemiah 8:10; Psalm 100:1-2). Even failures become laughter.',
        'Order + public repair (the Choir-Member-A / Member-B moment): grabbing a lane that isn’t yours pulls the true leader out of his flow and confuses the room — “God is not the author of confusion... decently and in order” (1 Corinthians 14:33,40). Remedy: honor/submit to the leadership God set (Hebrews 13:17; 1 Peter 5:5; Ephesians 5:21); and public offense gets public repair, forgiveness sought out loud by name — to LOVE, never to humiliate (James 5:16; Matthew 5:23-24; Galatians 6:1).',
