      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): pray, then read Mark 10:43-45 and Galatians 5:22-23 aloud — ask, “where does strife usually get into a team?” | The big idea, in your own words (10): name why music (and any gifting) is a magnet for pride, and the one move that keeps it out — “this is the Lord’s, not mine.” | Go deeper — the servant-king and the equal weight (10): walk Romans 8:6-7 (spiritual vs carnal mind), 1 Corinthians 12:18 / Psalm 127:1 (God grants the gelling), Matthew 7:1-2,12 + Proverbs 20:10 (accountability without the double standard), Mark 10:43-45 (the greatest servant is the king). | Reflect together (10): use the discussion prompts; be honest about where frustration or a double standard has crept in. | Take it with you (2): each person names the “won’t gel” thing and hands the outcome to God, then picks one servant task to do themselves — and, if needed, one public repair to make.',
